Reapply "[gc] Defer CalculationValue handle decrements from ~Length()"
(crbug 574686297, merge bug 577337360; no CVE listed yet): ~Length() could
run during Oilpan's sweeping and touch heap objects, which is not allowed
then (a use-after-free class of bug); the decrements are now queued and
flushed later. chromium/src main commit
218a524b0ed8ca8b6bbe7b02b818cdd65dea6ca5 (main@{#1726925}), merged on
2026-10-30 to 156 as 239f5a19d2f20c065e8cffaec142e3d67e02147a (after the
156.0.8078.84 tag); the 157 merge (Gerrit CL 8691925) was still open. This is that CL's patch (patch set 67007aa76fd5), the same lines as the 156
merge. Check the merged commit when it lands; drop this once a 157 tag has
it.

